From: Dustin Kirkland <dustin.kirkland@chainguard.dev>
Subject: cfPDFPagesFP: flush the temp file before PDFio opens it

Backport of upstream e14bad4 ("Fix printing error: pdfio output
\"Missing Root object.\" (#167)") with the error check from e7356ce
("Check temp file writes before PDFio reads them", fixes #284). Without
it, cfFilterGhostscript reports "Unexpected page count" for small PDFs
and every PDF -> PWG/URF raster job fails.
---
diff --git a/cupsfilters/pdf.c b/cupsfilters/pdf.c
index 1f714b2..fb945b3 100644
--- a/cupsfilters/pdf.c
+++ b/cupsfilters/pdf.c
@@ -165,6 +165,16 @@ cfPDFPagesFP(FILE *file) 	// I - File pointer of PDF
     fwrite(buffer, 1, bytes_read, temp_fp);
   }
 
+  // Flush the stdio buffer before PDFio reopens the file by name; otherwise
+  // a small PDF is still (partly) buffered and pdfioFileOpen() fails.
+  if (fflush(temp_fp) != 0)
+  {
+    fprintf(stderr, "fflush: Could not write temporary file\n");
+    fclose(temp_fp);
+    unlink(temp_filename);
+    return (-1);
+  }
+
   // Open the temp file with pdfio
   pdfio_file_t *pdf = pdfioFileOpen(temp_filename, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL);
 
